## Summary

Internal Audit tested required-training assignments and completions for all six sites against POL-CT-001 v3.2, MAT-ROLE-2026 and the LMS completion data. Four findings were raised: three high severity and one medium severity. Overall completion of required training across {{ org.short }} was 94.1% (target 98%).

## Findings

{% for f in audit_2026_q2.findings %}### {{ f.id }} ({{ f.severity }} severity, site {{ f.site }})

{{ f.text }}

Corrective action owner: {{ f.owner }}. Target date: {{ f.due }}.

{% if f.id == "F-1" %}Root cause: the clinic onboarded 38 per-diem staff in February 2026 through a staffing agency whose workers were not loaded into HRIS, so the LMS never assigned EHS-BBP-100. Recommended action: load agency staff into HRIS within 2 business days of start, and have the clinic manager confirm BBP completion before scheduling exposure-prone shifts.
{% elif f.id == "F-2" %}Root cause: the badge-suspension integration described in SOP-LMS-021 section 3.1 failed silently after the access control system upgrade in November 2025. Recommended action: restore the integration, add a daily reconciliation report of active badges without a current EHS-FL-201, and re-evaluate the 11 operators immediately.
{% elif f.id == "F-3" %}Root cause: the new job code was created in HRIS without a change request to Learning Systems. Recommended action: add PRV-HIP-110 and PRV-HIP-120 to CLN-TEL, assign them to the 18 employees with a 14-day due date, and require a curriculum review for every new job code before activation.
{% elif f.id == "F-4" %}Root cause: the v3.2 harassment scope change was implemented for new hires but not back-filled for existing employees outside California, New York, Illinois and Connecticut. Recommended action: run a one-time assignment for all U.S. employees without an HR-HAR-100 or HR-HAR-200 completion in the last 24 months.
{% endif %}
{% endfor %}
## Management Response

EHS and Learning Systems accepted all findings. The CLN-TEL dynamic group rule was corrected on 2026-07-10 (SOP-LMS-014 5.2).
